{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Coincidences", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "That's Bizarre!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the active voice when you want the \u2018doer' of the action to be the subject.<br/>You use the passive voice when you want the \u2018receiver' of the action to be the subject.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = The Porshe (subject) <span class=\"strong\">hit</span> the car (object).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Passive sentence = The car (subject) <span class=\"strong\"> was hit</span>  by a Porshe. (object).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It is not always necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\">be</span> verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Present passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "am/are/is + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">The man was found on top of the freeway sign.</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Past passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "was/were + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">The accident was filmed by someone's cell phone.</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It was reported two days ago.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You know that huge freeway sign that was built last year.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He was thrown from the vehicle. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The man was found by police.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience.<br/>When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Have you ever been in a car accident?<br/><br/>             Yes, I have (been in a car accident).</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Have you ever seen a car accident?<br/><br/>            No, I have never seen a car accident.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Have you ever driven on the 6 before?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've driven on the 6 more often than you have.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Have you ever had the lobster here?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was not the craziest story I have ever heard.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "just kidding", "type": "name"}, {"content": "you use this expression when you don't really mean what you are saying", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is not fit for people to eat. Just kidding!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about a traffic accident.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "highway", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a main road, especially one between towns or cities", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, you know highway 6, right? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to flip", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to turn over ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The young man's car flipped.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "seatbelt", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an arrangement of straps designed to keep a vehicle's passenger firmly secure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He wasn't wearing a seatbelt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "vehicle", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a thing that is used for transporting people or goods from one place to another, such as a car or lorry/truck", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He was thrown from the vehicle.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "force", "type": "name"}, {"content": "physical power or strength", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The force of the accident.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to toss", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to throw, especially lightly or carelessly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The force of the accident combined with the speed he was driving tossed him up onto the sign.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bet on that", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to express sarcasm, or to show disagreement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I would not bet on that.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "The teacher presents the final sentence of a strange event or happening.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In pairs, students must write a short story leading up to the final sentence that explains what happened.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present the stories to a group or the class.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Later, exchange stories with other groups and check each others for grammar errors.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "After, the papers are returned to the students and the grammar is corrected.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about coincidences and strange events. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can analyze sentences for appropriate grammar points.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about coincidences and strange events. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can discuss experiences I have and haven't had.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can react and comment on a story.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Have you ever been in a car accident? If yes, what happened?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "How can traffic accidents be prevented?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:",